&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49842079</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:25:11 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Proxima Forma – Designs that my AI agents understand</title><link>https://proximaforma.com/</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hey HN!&lt;p&gt;I built Proxima Forma because sharing screenshots with my agents was not really doing the job. I am a UX Designer with a developer background so I needed a better tool.&lt;p&gt;Wanted the agents to have full design history, design decisions, product notes, etc. in a format they could actually understand.&lt;p&gt;Also wanted one place to manage all my design projects, with dynamic views that let me query projects to see the latest changes and exactly what changed.&lt;p&gt;And wanted to do all that from the commodity of my iPad ;) -early tries of using voice agents to design are still in progress, spoiler: it is too slow... But we'll get there with better models or more fine tuning.&lt;p&gt;Any feedback from the community is really appreciated.&lt;p&gt;I'm trying to come up with other uses cases for Proxima Forma, not only UX Design.&lt;p&gt;In a side note: fully built with AI Agents, Astra, and a little of Meta AI -for instagram advice.&lt;p&gt;Cheers
